                text: "Everyone faces adversity at some point in their lives, but how we respond to these unexpected challenges truly defines who we are. Last year, my incredibly smart best friend Julia experienced a terrible setback when she failed her university entrance exams. She had been studying tirelessly for months, waking up early and skipping social events, so the failure left her feeling completely overwhelmed and defeated. In fact, she told me that she wanted to give up entirely and call off her ambitious plans for higher education. I listened to her cry, but I knew that persistence is key to overcoming any hardship, isn't it? I wondered if I could help her see the situation differently. I reminded her that time is precious and that every mistake is simply a valuable lesson in disguise. I suggested that we should call in a professional tutor to help her focus on her weak subjects. She eventually agreed, and we carried out a strict study plan together. Julia’s mother also told her that she had to embrace her mistakes rather than run from them. With renewed strength and resilience, Julia took the exams again the following year and carried off a brilliant score. Her inspiring story proves that we must consistently strive for our goals, no matter what obstacles get in our way.",
